<article class="env-remark" id="02ER">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02ER">Remark <span data-tag="02ER">111.29.4</span>.</a> Let $h \in {\mathbf Z}[y]$ be a monic polynomial of degree $d$. Then: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The map $A = {\mathbf Z}[x] \to B ={\mathbf Z}[y]$, $x \mapsto h$ is finite locally free of rank $d$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For all primes $p$ the map $A_ p = {\mathbf F}_ p[x]\to B_ p = {\mathbf F}_ p[y]$, $y \mapsto h(y) \bmod p$ is finite locally free of rank $d$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>